# Practice Tracker: Architecture & Cloud Guide (In Simple Words)

This guide explains the entire **Practice Tracker** system, how every piece works, what we built in the cloud, why we need each piece, and how they talk to each other — using simple, everyday language and analogies.

---

## 1. The Big Picture: The Restaurant Analogy

To understand how the system works without getting lost in technical terms, think of **Practice Tracker** like a high-end restaurant:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        THE PRACTICE TRACKER SYSTEM                     │
├────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬────────────────┤
│  1. Mobile App     │  2. Cloud Run (The Kitchen)      │  3. Cloud SQL  │
│  (The Customer)    │                                  │  (The Ledger)  │
│                    │  • Core API: Head Waiter/Manager │                │
│  You record your   │  • Worker-Poly: Piano/Chord Chef │  Permanent,    │
│  music on your     │  • Worker-Mono: Solo Voice Chef  │  secure        │
│  phone and order   │                                  │  database of   │
│  an analysis       │  Listens to the audio, figures   │  users, scores │
│                    │  out the notes, scores pitch &   │  and practice  │
│                    │  timing                          │  history       │
└────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴────────────────┘
```

1. **The Mobile App (The Customer)**: You record your violin, voice, or piano on your phone. You tap "Analyze". You are placing an order for a musical critique.
2. **The Core API (The Head Waiter / Manager)**: The waiter welcomes you, checks your table reservation (login/password), writes down your order in the book, and decides which chef should cook your meal.
3. **The ML Workers (The Specialized Chefs)**:
   - **Chef Poly (`worker-poly`)**: Specializes in complex multi-note feasts (Piano, Guitar, chords).
   - **Chef Mono (`worker-mono`)**: Specializes in delicate single melodies (Voice, Violin, Flute).
4. **Cloud SQL (The Secure Bookkeeper / Filing Cabinet)**: Keeps a permanent record of all users, every session you practiced, and your scores so you can see your progress over time.
5. **Artifact Registry (The Blueprint Locker)**: Holds the exact software containers (recipes) so the cloud can launch copies of the servers whenever needed.

