## 5. Why Did We Use the Cloud? (Why Not Just Keep It on the Laptop or Phone?)

| Problem Without Cloud | How Our Cloud Solution Solves It |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Phones are too weak for big AI models** | Running TensorFlow, Basic Pitch, and CREPE directly on a phone would make the phone burning hot, drain the battery in 20 minutes, and make the app download size over 600 MB. The cloud runs it on powerful multi-core server CPUs in 2 seconds. |
| **Laptops sleep & change IP addresses** | If you run the server on your laptop, the moment you close your laptop lid or leave your Wi-Fi, the mobile app stops working. Cloud Run is awake 24/7/365 worldwide. |
| **Expensive servers that run 24/7** | Traditional cloud servers (like AWS EC2 or Virtual Machines) bill you every single hour even when nobody is using them. **Cloud Run is serverless**: if nobody is practicing at 3 AM, it scales down to **zero** and costs **$0.00**. It only turns on when a musician uploads audio. |
| **Data safety & backups** | If your laptop disk crashes, all your database history is gone. **Cloud SQL** is automatically backed up, replicated, and protected by Google's multi-tier storage redundancy. |

